        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0898" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">311.6124/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Young</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-12T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Department of Labor has just informed State Department that arrangements were
                    made by one of its representatives with the Latvian representative in New York
                    for transit through Latvia of twenty-four aliens who sailed from New York
                    December 23, 1920, via S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Imperator</hi>, and that
                    these deportees were transshipped to Libau, <pb facs="0899" n="803"
                        xml:id="pg803"/> where they were met by representatives of Latvia, placed
                    aboard a train and taken to Riga, and turned over to Soviet representatives.</p>
                <p>If any complications arose, cable facts briefly; otherwise submit full report by
                    mail.</p>
                <p>Do you perceive any objection to future similar informal arrangements by Labor
                    Department?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
